Z||000000||beachbomb||07-16-2001||11:51 AM||||Hi all, well my worst fear came true, the cam gear or camshaft is now borke on my Indy, my question to you all is..... is it easier to fix this by pulling the engine or dropping the engine from the bottom partially and fixing it this way, plmk, i know this will be a big pain in the a**, but i need to get my car back on the road, thanks jim||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cozmo||07-16-2001||01:43 PM||||There are two ways to do this, the way you suggested and replacing the gear while the cam is still in the car.<BR>  I just did one recently by dropping the rear of the cradle enough to pull the camshaft out of the passengers side wheel well. It was tedious but not too difficult, did it in a weekend.<BR>   Some people suggest just cutting off the old gear and then heating the new gear in a pan of oil in the oven at 400 deg. for 20 min.  Then supposedly it just slips right on.<BR>  I didn't feel comfortable with this method, so I did it by the book.  If you search  the archives there is a ton of info on this problem.<BR>Good luck!!!<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR>PS get the metal gear set instead of the nylon ones...||||reg||1
Z||000002||beachbomb||07-16-2001||08:02 PM||||Hey cozmo, i emailed you some questions, thanks, also i notice you're in Fl, maybe you can come up here and tech assist me(HEHEHE!!)..thanks..jim||||reg||5
